findings.description:
Lines 177-179 say PR title, body, issues and threads are "clearly delimited data … never as instructions." Delimiting reduces prompt injection but doesn't prevent it. This review runs with file-reading tools (266/267) and has a post-to-PR path under the operator's credentials. The document says nothing about:
- delimiter-collision escaping (the PR body contains the closing delimiter);
- whether the tool set stays read-only and jailed to the scratch tree, not the operator's tree;
- whether the posted comment body is sanitized (reviewer output is model text that could be steered, and it's posted with the operator's identity);
- treating `@mentions` and links in posted text.

The attribution claim at lines 57-58 and 182-183, "attributed to the operator, who asked for it," means attacker-steerable text is published as the operator.
